Author:&nbsp;<a href="/showmember.php?name=Kenari">Kenari</a>&nbsp;(---.ballistic.com)<br>
Date:&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;05-08-01 13:54<br>
<br>There were others there that could have helped. As everyone that attended knows, I wasn't there. But I was watching. And there were players who could have helped. The thing is, No one is required to help at all. But as part of the guild, and one of honor at that, we should help each other when possible. In a raid, we always want as many participants as possible. A big part of any raid includes making sure all participating members are present. If help is needed after a death then so be it. I know that the worst part of this game is waiting. Waiting to get a group together, waiting to mem spells, waiting for others to get corpses, and waiting for a dead member to return. It sucks...but it is necessary... for the guild, the raid, and the game. &lt;P&gt; Before a raid is scheduled to start, anyone who wishes to participate should get a map from the book or a web site ( see links to the left ). They should get there character there, and get a bind at the closest available place. If need be do it early then camp and come back at specified time. This is suggested for events, such as weddings and meetings, as well as raids. This should be a huge help as to the topic of organization. &lt;P&gt; Sorry so wordy, just my 2cp! :) &lt;P&gt; ~K</font></tt><p>
